"Aaron and Vanessa were relay race partners on a running team. Aaron was able to run each mile twice as fast as Vanessa, but Vanessa was able to run twice as far as Aaron did. If Vanessa ran 4 miles and Aaron barely completed his part of the race in 16 minutes, how long in minutes did Vanessa take to complete her part?","Aaron and Vanessa were relay race partners on a running team. Aaron was able to run each mile twice as fast as Vanessa, but Vanessa was able to run twice as far as Aaron did. If Vanessa ran 4 miles and Aaron completed his part of the race in 16 minutes, how long in minutes did Vanessa take to complete her part?",64,64,64,64,"Let's define variables:

- Let v be Vanessa’s speed (miles per minute).
- Then Aaron’s speed is 2v (since Aaron runs each mile twice as fast as Vanessa).
- Vanessa runs twice as far as Aaron. Given Vanessa ran 4 miles, Aaron ran 2 miles.

Aaron’s time:
- Distance = 2 miles, Speed = 2v
- Time = distance / speed = 2 / (2v) = 1/v minutes
- Given Aaron’s time is 16 minutes, so 1/v = 16 → v = 1/16 miles per minute.

Vanessa’s time:
- Distance = 4 miles, Speed = v = 1/16 miles per minute
- Time = 4 / (1/16) = 4 × 16 = 64 minutes

