- 30 students × 10 pencils each = 300 pencils

Step 2: After two months, 1/5 of the total pencils were used.
- Used: (1/5) × 300 = 60
- Remaining: 300 − 60 = 240

Step 3: At the end of the year, 1/3 of the remaining pencils were lost.
- Lost: (1/3) × 240 = 80
- Final remaining: 240 − 80 = 160

