"Peter plans to go to the movies this week. He never gets a ticket for anything but $7 and popcorn for anything but $7. If he has 42 dollars for the week, how many times can he go to the movies?","Peter plans to go to the movies this week. He always gets a ticket for $7 and popcorn for $7. If he has 42 dollars for the week, how many times can he go to the movies?",3,3,3,3,"Let’s define the costs and total budget.

- Each movie outing consists of a ticket and popcorn.
- Peter never gets a ticket for anything but $7 and popcorn for anything but $7.
- So, cost per outing = $7 (ticket) + $7 (popcorn) = $14.
- Total budget for the week = $42.

Now, calculate how many full outings he can afford:
- Number of outings = $42 ÷ $14 = 3.

